@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why the posture is one value rendered twice, and why nothing here decides anything
' covers: internal/posture/posture.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/posture_golden_test.go
'
' ── THE BUG THAT MADE IT A PACKAGE ─────────────────────────────────────────
' A run states its posture twice: the header a human reads BEFORE launch, and the
' run-log block a human reads AFTER a failure. Those were assembled independently,
' so they could disagree about the same run — and did: a row named Squid logs on a
' backend that runs no Squid. Two renderings of one value cannot disagree; two
' assemblies of the same idea always eventually do.
'
' ── NOTHING HERE DECIDES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Every input arrives as a VALUE. Posture never reads env, never probes docker,
' never consults a manifest. That is the whole discipline: the moment a row can
' work out its own answer, the row becomes a second place the decision is made,
' and the header stops being a report of the run and starts being a claim about
' it. Observability, EnforcedBy, MCPGateway and ResolveImageChoice all take what
' they need as arguments for exactly this reason.
'
' ── WHAT THE GOLDENS PIN ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
' cmd/proveo/posture_golden_test.go renders both backends and pins the bytes. The
' wording differs per backend on purpose ("proveo runs no Squid or MITM" against
' "squid + mitmproxy sidecars"), and that difference is the thing most likely to
' rot silently, because nothing else fails when a row describes the wrong backend.
'
' ── KNOWN OVERSTATEMENT, DELIBERATELY LEFT ─────────────────────────────────
' EnforcedBy says "sbx — Kit network allowlist + credential proxy" whatever sbx's
' global baseline is. On an allow-all host that allowlist ADDS reach rather than
' limiting it, so the row overstates. It is left standing and recorded here rather
' than quietly fixed: the same finding governs decision D2, and the egress row
' already tells the operator the truth at the point of choosing
' (_spec/internal/sbx/policy-baseline.puml).
title internal/posture — one value, two readers, no decisions

participant "run.buildPosture" as RUN <<app>>
participant "posture.Posture" as P <<data>>
participant "header\n(before launch)" as H <<app>>
participant "run log\n(after failure)" as L <<data>>

RUN ARROW_MAIN P : every field as a VALUE
P ARROW_MAIN H : Render()
P ARROW_MAIN L : Fields()

note over P
  **A row may not compute its answer.** Give it
  the value. A row that can decide is a second
  place the decision is made, and the two readers
  drift apart again.
end note
@enduml
